---
import LegalPage from '../components/LegalPage.astro';
import site from '../data/site.json';
const { email, phone, address } = site.contact;
---
<LegalPage
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="How Lobi Stars FC collects and uses personal data on this website."
  updated="22 October 2026"
>
  <p>This policy explains what personal data Lobi Stars Football Club ("the club", "we") collects through lobistarsfc.com, why, and your rights under the Nigeria Data Protection Act 2023 (NDPA).</p>

  <h2>1. Who we are</h2>
  <p>Lobi Stars Football Club, {address}. Email <a href={`mailto:${email}`}>{email}</a>, phone {phone}. Contact us at these details for any privacy question or request.</p>

  <h2>2. What we collect and why</h2>
  <div class="lg-scroll"><table>
    <thead><tr><th>When you…</th><th>We collect</th><th>Why</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td>Create a fan account</td><td>First name, surname, email, phone number, password (stored only in scrambled/hashed form), confirmation that you are 18+, and whether you want news and offers</td><td>To run your account, confirm your email, and let you vote and play Predict &amp; Win</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Vote for Man of the Match</td><td>Which player you voted for, for which match, and when</td><td>To count votes fairly (one per fan) and show the results</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Play Predict &amp; Win</td><td>Your predicted score, the match, and the exact time we received it</td><td>To find the winner (earliest exact prediction), contact them and prevent fraud. The winner's first name, surname initial and a partly hidden phone number are shown publicly on the match page</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Become a member</td><td>The details on the membership form</td><td>To manage your membership</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Buy tickets or order food</td><td>Name, email, phone, order and seat details. Card payments are handled by Paystack; we never see your card details</td><td>To issue tickets, deliver orders and keep accounting records</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Order food on WhatsApp</td><td>Name, phone, seat or pickup point, your order and note. The order message is sent by you through WhatsApp to the club's number, so WhatsApp's own terms also apply</td><td>To confirm your order, arrange payment and deliver it. Kitchen staff only see your first name, your seat or pickup point and the food</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Join the newsletter</td><td>Name, email address, phone number and the newsletter options you choose (weekly newsletter, matchday and ticket alerts, partner offers)</td><td>To send the newsletter and the alerts you asked for. Every email has an unsubscribe link and a link to change your options. Clicks on links in the newsletter are counted (not linked to you) to show sponsors how their adverts perform</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Turn on match alerts</td><td>No name, email or phone. Only the notification address your browser gives us (a random link from your browser's push service), the alert types you chose and when you turned them on</td><td>To send the match notifications you asked for. Turn them off on the same box at any time, or block notifications for this site in your browser; addresses that stop working are switched off automatically</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Contact us or send a partnership or hospitality enquiry</td><td>Name, email, phone, company, your message and our replies</td><td>To reply to you by email and keep the conversation together so any staff member can help</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Read the Match Day Programme</td><td>Your email address, first name, and optionally your surname and phone number; which programmes you open, which pages you view, downloads and quick-link clicks, and where you came from (for example a QR code at the gate)</td><td>To give registered fans access to the programme, send club news only if you tick the box, and count total readers for the club and its sponsors. See "Match Day Programme" below</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Join Lobi Stars Rewards</td><td>That you joined, when, the version of the Rewards Terms you accepted, and your member number (for example LSR-000123)</td><td>To run your Rewards membership. See "Lobi Stars Rewards" below</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Complete your Rewards profile (optional)</td><td>Your state of residence and date of birth</td><td>To give the one-off profile bonus and the birthday bonus. We also use the state for anonymous totals (for example how many members live in Benue)</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Earn or use Star Points</td><td>A history of every points change: what it was for (for example a ticket order, a gate scan at a home match, a Man of the Match vote, a prediction, reading the programme or a referral), the points, and when</td><td>To add and take away points correctly, work out your tier, and show you your history</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Invite a friend</td><td>Who invited whom, and whether the referral was rewarded or held back</td><td>To give referral points fairly and stop people inviting themselves</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Create a fan account</td><td>A random ID for the browser you signed up on (not your IP address or device details)</td><td>To spot several accounts created on one device, so referral and bonus points are not abused</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Redeem a reward</td><td>The reward, the points used, any voucher code and when it was used, the match chosen for a reward ticket, and any note you give us for an experience or item</td><td>To deliver your reward, check vouchers at the stadium and club shop, and handle problems</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Pay with Star Points or a voucher</td><td>The points or voucher used on the order</td><td>To take the right amount and give points back if the payment fails or is refunded</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Choose Rewards messages</td><td>Which Rewards emails you want, and the messages we show on My Rewards (and whether you have read them)</td><td>To send only the emails you chose</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Choose to appear on the Legend Fans wall (optional)</td><td>Your choice</td><td>To show your <strong>first name and surname initial</strong> publicly on the <a href="/rewards/legend-fans/">Legend Fans wall</a>. You can stop at any time</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Order a personalised shirt</td><td>Name and number to print, size, your name, email and phone, and the time you confirmed that personalised shirts can't be returned or refunded (unless faulty or printed wrongly)</td><td>To make and deliver your shirt and keep a record of the agreement</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Download the partnership brochure</td><td>Name, email, company and phone (optional), and whether you want updates</td><td>To follow up on partnership interest</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table></div>

  <h3>Our fan database</h3>
  <p>To avoid contacting the same person twice, we combine records that share the same email address or phone number into one contact record, showing how you have engaged with the club (for example newsletter, tickets, Predict &amp; Win). Only authorised club staff can see it; downloads are restricted and every download is logged.</p>

  <h3 id="rewards">Lobi Stars Rewards</h3>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Joining is your choice.</strong> Rewards is free and optional. You can use the website, buy tickets and play Predict &amp; Win without joining.</li>
    <li><strong>Your member card</strong> on My Rewards shows a QR code. It contains only your member number and a security code, <strong>no name, email or phone</strong>. Club staff scan it at the stadium food stands and club shop to see the vouchers you can use.</li>
    <li><strong>Tiers and badges</strong> are worked out from your points history. They are not shared outside the club.</li>
    <li><strong>Fraud checks.</strong> To keep the programme fair, club staff see a list of accounts worth checking (for example several accounts created on one device, many points earned in a week, or points taken back after refunds). A person always checks before any action. If your membership is put on hold, you can contact us to explain.</li>
    <li><strong>Reports.</strong> Staff see totals (members, points issued and used, members per tier). Downloads that include personal data are restricted to authorised staff and every download is logged. Sponsors and partners <strong>never</strong> receive your personal data, only anonymous totals.</li>
    <li><strong>Messages.</strong> We show Rewards messages on My Rewards. We email you only the kinds you chose under "Email me about", except emails you ask for directly (such as your voucher code or a sign-in code).</li>
    <li><strong>Leaving.</strong> You can leave Rewards or ask us to delete your Rewards data at any time by contacting us. Your Star Points end when you leave; they have no cash value.</li>
  </ul>

  <h3 id="programme">Match Day Programme</h3>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Signing in:</strong> you sign in with a 6-digit code sent to your email; no password is needed. This uses (or creates) your free Lobi Stars fan account, so the same login works for Man of the Match and Predict &amp; Win. Codes are stored only in scrambled (hashed) form and expire after 10 minutes. You stay signed in on that device for up to 90 days unless you sign out.</li>
    <li><strong>Reading activity:</strong> we record which programme and pages you open, downloads and quick-link clicks, linked to your account, so the club knows how the programme is used. Sponsors only ever receive total, anonymous numbers (for example "2,300 readers"); <strong>your personal data is never given to sponsors</strong>.</li>
    <li><strong>QR codes:</strong> when you scan one of our QR adverts (e.g. lobistarsfc.com/p/gate) we count the scan for that advert, with only the kind of device (Android, iPhone or computer) and whether it opened inside an app such as Facebook. We do not store your IP address or browser details for this. If you then sign in, we note which advert brought you, so the club knows which adverts work.</li>
    <li><strong>Shared links:</strong> programme links the club or fans share on social media (lobistarsfc.com/m/…) count visits per platform (for example "Facebook" or "WhatsApp"), anonymously, in the same way as QR codes.</li>
    <li><strong>Club news:</strong> only if you tick "Send me club news and match day programme alerts" (never ticked for you). We store the date you agreed, and you can unsubscribe at any time.</li>
    <li><strong>On your device:</strong> programme pages you read may be saved in your browser so you can read them without a connection; signing out removes them.</li>
    <li><strong>How long:</strong> your account while it is open; reading activity for up to 2 years, then deleted or made anonymous.</li>
    <li><strong>Delete my data:</strong> use "Delete my data" on the <a href="/programme/">programme page</a> or email us; we confirm by email and then delete your data everywhere.</li>
  </ul>

  <h3 id="squad-profiles">Player and staff profiles</h3>
  <p><em>Draft for legal review.</em> This part is for Lobi Stars players, coaches and staff. The club's media team collects your profile details in the club's private Squad &amp; Staff Data Portal, with your agreement.</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>What we collect:</strong> your surname, first name and middle name as on your passport or official ID, date of birth, place of birth, nationality (and any second nationality or national team), state of origin and hometown, playing or staff details (position, shirt number, role, height, preferred foot, previous clubs, international career, honours, coaching licence), photos, an interesting fact about you, optional Instagram, X and TikTok handles and media notes, and, for club records only, your phone, email and an emergency contact. For anyone under 18, the details and consent of a parent or guardian. The club may add a short biography, your Lobi Stars debut date and a link to buy your shirt.</li>
    <li><strong>What is public:</strong> on lobistarsfc.com (the Squad pages) we show your name, photos, position or role, shirt number, nationality, place of birth, height, preferred foot, career history, international career, honours, biography, interesting fact and social handles where given. <strong>If you are 18 or over</strong>, also your full name (including middle name) and your date of birth; <strong>if you are under 18</strong>, only your age and first name and surname. Your phone, email, emergency contact and guardian details are <strong>never</strong> published.</li>
    <li><strong>Match coverage and broadcasts:</strong> so that you are introduced and named correctly, the club shares your public details, photos and media notes with the club's appointed media partner, which produces live match coverage and broadcasts of Lobi Stars games. The partner receives no private details and may use the information only for covering Lobi Stars matches.</li>
    <li><strong>Why (legal basis):</strong> your consent, which you give when the profile is submitted (and that of a parent or guardian for under-18s), and the club's legitimate interest in keeping accurate squad and staff records. You can withdraw consent for publication at any time; the public profile is then removed.</li>
    <li><strong>Who can see the private details:</strong> only the club staff who review profiles and the club's Super Admins. Downloads with private details are limited to Super Admins, need a sign-in code and are logged.</li>
    <li><strong>How long:</strong> while you are with the club. When you leave, your profile is marked "left the club" and taken off the website; your private details are erased <strong>2 seasons after you leave</strong>. A short public record (name, position, seasons and honours) may be kept as club history.</li>
    <li><strong>Your rights:</strong> you can ask to see, correct or delete your profile details by contacting the club's media team or <a href={`mailto:${email}`}>{email}</a>.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>3. Marketing</h2>
  <p>We only send news and offers by email or SMS if you have said yes. Every marketing email has an unsubscribe link, and you can also ask us to stop at any time. Important messages about your account, tickets, orders or a prize are still sent.</p>
  <p>If you said yes to news and offers on your fan account, this can include reminders such as "Predictions are now open" and "Kick-off: vote for Man of the Match" for home games.</p>

  <h2 id="cookies">4. Cookies and website statistics</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Essential:</strong> a login cookie keeps you signed in to your fan account (up to 30 days), and your cookie choice is remembered in your browser. These are needed for the site to work.</li>
    <li><strong>Statistics:</strong> we count page views to improve the site. If you <em>reject</em> non-essential cookies we only count anonymous page views. If you <em>accept</em>, a random ID in your browser lets us recognise returning visitors. We do not store IP addresses, and we use no advertising cookies.</li>
    <li><strong>Google Analytics (only if you accept):</strong> if you press <em>Accept</em>, we also use Google Analytics 4 to understand how the site is used: which pages are visited, how visitors arrive (for example from Google search or social media), the type of device, the approximate city or country, and general actions such as starting a ticket purchase, placing a food order, signing up to the newsletter, joining our WhatsApp Channel or submitting a prediction. Google Analytics sets cookies (named <code>_ga</code>) for this. We never send Google your name, phone number, email address, payment details or what you ordered, and we switch off Google's advertising features. Google does not keep IP addresses in Google Analytics 4. If you <em>reject</em>, Google Analytics is not loaded at all, and choosing Reject later removes its cookies. Google LLC processes this data for us; see <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google's Privacy Policy</a>.</li>
    <li><strong>Share buttons:</strong> the Share buttons on our pages use no third-party trackers or social media scripts; when you choose a share option we count the click anonymously (only the page and the platform, for example "WhatsApp").</li>
    <li>Change your choice any time with <strong>Cookie settings</strong> at the bottom of every page.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>5. Who we share data with</h2>
  <p>We do not sell your data. We use trusted service providers who process data for us:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Cloudflare</strong>: website hosting and database, and the optional "human check" on forms.</li>
    <li><strong>Resend</strong>: sending emails.</li>
    <li><strong>Paystack</strong>: card payments.</li>
    <li><strong>Formspree</strong>: delivering contact and partnership form messages to the club's inbox.</li>
    <li><strong>YouTube / Facebook</strong>: live streams. The video player only loads when you press play, and those sites' own privacy policies then apply.</li>
    <li><strong>Google Fonts</strong>: the website's fonts.</li>
    <li><strong>The club's media partner</strong>: public details of players and staff only, for match coverage (see "Player and staff profiles").</li>
  </ul>
  <p>Some of these providers may process data outside Nigeria; we rely on appropriate safeguards as required by the NDPA.</p>

  <h2>6. How long we keep data</h2>
  <p>We keep personal data only as long as needed for the purposes above: account data while your account is open, Predict &amp; Win and payment records as long as needed for accounting and to resolve disputes, and marketing data until you unsubscribe. When you ask us to delete your data we delete it everywhere, except payment records, which we keep for accounting with your name and contact details removed.</p>
  <p><strong>Lobi Stars Rewards:</strong> your membership details and points history while you have a fan account. Points expire after 12 months with no activity, but the history stays so you can see it. If you ask us to delete your data, your Rewards membership, messages and referral links are deleted, and your points history and redeemed rewards are kept only as anonymous totals (no longer linked to you). The random sign-up browser ID is kept with your fan account and deleted with it.</p>

  <h2>7. Your rights</h2>
  <p>Under the NDPA you can ask us to: give you a copy of your data; correct it; delete it; stop marketing to you; restrict or object to how we use it; and withdraw any consent you gave. Contact us at <a href={`mailto:${email}`}>{email}</a>. If you are unhappy with how we handled your data you can complain to the Nigeria Data Protection Commission (NDPC).</p>

  <h2>8. Security and children</h2>
  <p>Passwords are stored only in hashed form, the site uses HTTPS, and staff access is restricted by individual logins. Fan accounts, voting, Predict &amp; Win and Lobi Stars Rewards are for people aged 18 and over. Some rewards (for example those from alcohol sponsors) have their own minimum age.</p>

  <h2>9. Changes</h2>
  <p>We will update this page if we change how we use personal data. The date at the top shows the latest version.</p>
</LegalPage>
